  message: "GRAMMAR-SWAP CHECK 2026-11-01 (owner asked to verify before any grammar change; artifacts ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/tracker_hygiene_sweep_2026-11-01T223538Z/agda_grammar_check/). WHAT THE TWO GRAMMARS ARE: PyPI tree-sitter-agda 1.3.3 = upstream tree-sitter/tree-sitter-agda tag v1.3.3 (47802091de, 2024-11-10). tree-sitter-language-pack 0.13.0 pins agda to the same repo at master e8d47a6987 (2025-08-30, from the pack's sources/language_definitions.json). The 1.3.3..e8d47a6987 diff is 3 files: publish.yml, tree-sitter.json (query paths) and src/scanner.c d44b342455 'fix(scanner): adjust container allocations' (the layout-token ring buffer was grown by realloc without re-linearising it, so queued newline/indent tokens land in the wrong slots after a wrap). Same ABI 14, identical 228 node kinds, 0 fields: agda.py's node-type branches see the same vocabulary. No reason for choosing the dedicated wheel is recorded (7b0a72d33c; both deps already existed then). FIXTURES: the pack parses this item's probes and WI-molon's fx_molon M/N (empty nested module) error-free; where the bundled grammar is error-free the trees are identical. CORPUS (agda-stdlib 1264 .agda + PLFA 40, shallow clones): files with parse errors 571->508 (stdlib); the pack never errors on a file 1.3.3 parses cleanly, but has MORE error nodes in 56 already-erroring files. Analyzer A/B on stdlib (AgdaAnalyzer vs a language_pack_name='agda' subclass, separate caches): symbols 23480->23596; real declarations GAINED 166 in 51 files; real declarations LOST 43 in 10 files (e.g. record IsMagma in src/Algebra/Structures.agda, Lattice/MeetSemilattice/BooleanAlgebra/DistributiveLattice records in src/Algebra/Lattice/Bundles.agda, LeftModule, Data/Integer Positive); scope chains deeper (correct, sampled) on 516 lines, shallower on 86; stable_id changes for 192 common symbols; 149 of 1265 files change. Junk-named symbols (e.g. a field named ':') are ~equal (316 vs 307), and ~40% of stdlib files error under EITHER grammar. VERDICT: the swap fixes this item's shapes but is a trade, not a strict improvement; it is not the fix for agda parse quality in general. Prerequisites if pursued: WI-siniv (extended1 does not declare the pack), and the pack's ~=0.13.0 pin would then also pin the agda revision. Owner decision; nothing changed."  # d2c2
